{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YU73kFjd5w6eg6KwTe7VRe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UfxjbA9ssShTvoSmfAFmMF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-10-2145-batch-degenerate-stacked-reduction/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Batch Degenerate Stacked Reduction Kernel Launches\n\n## Goal\n\nBatch all degenerate-window kernel launches within `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` into a single GPU kernel launch per round, eliminating ~10,348 tiny kernel launches (at APC 300) that contribute ~217ms of CPU-side launch/sync overhead. The degenerate case handles windows where `log_height < l_skip + round`, producing single-block kernels with `grid(1)`. Because all window results are summed at the end (line 909-911), they can be atomically accumulated into one shared output buffer by a single multi-block launch.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Call Chain\n\n1. `prove_stacked_opening_reduction_gpu` (`stacked_reduction.rs:185`) calls `prover.batch_sumcheck_poly_eval(round, u_prev)` for each MLE round 1..=n_stack (line 244).\n2. `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (`stacked_reduction.rs:793-912`):\n   - Lines 800-802: Collect `q_eval_ptrs` and upload to device.\n   - Lines 804-831: If applicable, D2H copy stable `eq_r` and `k_rot_r` values for the current round.\n   - Lines 832-907: **The per-window loop** (this is what we modify).\n   - Lines 909-911: Sum all per-window results: `s_evals_batch.iter().map(|evals| evals[i]).sum()`.\n\n### The Per-Window Loop (lines 832-907)\n\nFor each window in `ht_diff_idxs.windows(2)`:\n\n1. Compute `unstacked_cols_ptr` and `lambda_pows_ptr` from window offset (lines 836-839).\n2. Get `log_height` from first column in window (line 841).\n3. `d_accum.fill_zero()` — memset kernel (line 844-846).\n4. **Branch on degenerate condition** (`log_height < l_skip + round`):\n   - **Degenerate path** (lines 848-878):\n     - Get `eq_r = eq_stable[log_height]`, `k_rot_r = k_rot_stable[log_height]` (scalars, on host).\n     - H2D copy: `eq_ub_per_trace[window_start..window_end]` -> `d_eq_ub` (line 861).\n     - Kernel launch: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate(...)` with `grid(1), block(min(window_len, 256))` (line 864).\n   - **Non-degenerate path** (lines 879-901):\n     - Compute `num_y = 1 << (log_height - l_skip - round)`.\n     - Kernel launch: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round(...)` with auto-tuned grid.\n5. `d_accum.to_host()` — D2H copy + implicit sync via `cudaEventSynchronize` (line 904).\n6. `reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(&h_accum)` — reduce u64 accumulators modulo P (line 905).\n7. Push per-window result to `s_evals_batch` (line 906).\n\n### Why It's Slow\n\nEach degenerate window iteration involves 4 CUDA runtime API calls:\n1. `fill_zero()` -> `cudaMemsetAsync` (memset kernel)\n2. `copy_to()` -> `cudaMemcpyAsync` (H2D for eq_ub slice)\n3. Kernel launch -> `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_kernel<<<grid(1), block(...)>>>`\n4. `to_host()` -> `cudaMemcpyAsync` (D2H) + `cudaEventSynchronize` (blocking sync)\n\nAt APC 300, there are ~10,348 degenerate windows per round. Nsight profiling shows GPU kernel time is ~93ms but wall-clock is 310ms. The ~217ms gap (70%) is CPU-side CUDA runtime overhead from issuing and synchronizing 10,348+ tiny operations sequentially.\n\n### Key Properties\n\n- **All window results are summed**: `from_fn(|i| s_evals_batch.iter().map(|evals| evals[i]).sum())` (line 909-911). This means all degenerate contributions can be accumulated into a single output buffer via atomics.\n- **Windows are independent**: No data dependencies between windows. Each reads from its own slice of `unstacked_cols`, `lambda_pows`, and `eq_ub_per_trace`.\n- **Existing kernel already uses atomics**: The degenerate kernel calls `sumcheck::atomic_add_fpext_to_u64(output + idx * 4, reduced)` (stacked_reduction.cu:364). Multiple blocks writing to the same output is safe.\n- **Overflow is not a risk**: 10,348 blocks x max 256 threads x ~2^31 per component < 2^45 << 2^64.\n- **`unstacked_cols` and `lambda_pows` are already on device**: `d_unstacked_cols` and `d_lambda_pows` are uploaded once in `StackedReductionGpu::new()` (lines 393, 391). We only need to pass per-window offsets.\n- **`eq_ub_per_trace` is on host only**: Must be gathered and uploaded for degenerate windows.\n- **`FpExt`/`bb31_4_t` has 4-byte natural alignment**: `__align__(16)` was explicitly removed from `bb31_4_t` (see `crates/cuda-common/include/ff/baby_bear.hpp:75`). This means `#[repr(C)]` structs containing `FpExt` fields will pack identically on both Rust and CUDA sides without hidden padding.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Overview\n\nSplit the per-window loop into:\n1. **Classification**: Separate degenerate vs non-degenerate windows.\n2. **Batched degenerate path**: One `fill_zero` + one H2D + one kernel launch + one D2H for all degenerate windows.\n3. **Per-window non-degenerate path**: Keep existing logic (these already have auto-tuned multi-block launches with meaningful GPU work).\n\n### Step 1: Define `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (near `UnstackedSlice` definition, around line 150)\n\nAdd a new FFI-compatible struct:\n\n```rust\n/// Per-window metadata for the batched degenerate kernel.\n/// Must match the CUDA-side `DegenerateWindowMeta` layout exactly.\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\npub(crate) struct DegenerateWindowMeta {\n    /// Offset into the global `d_unstacked_cols` / `d_lambda_pows` arrays.\n    col_offset: u32,\n    /// Offset into the concatenated `d_eq_ub` buffer for this window's eq_ub values.\n    eq_ub_offset: u32,\n    /// Number of columns in this window.\n    window_len: u32,\n    /// Padding for alignment (keeps FpExt fields at 16-byte boundary).\n    _pad: u32,\n    /// Folded eq evaluation for this window's log_height: `eq_stable[log_height]`.\n    eq_r: EF,\n    /// Folded k_rot evaluation for this window's log_height: `k_rot_stable[log_height]`.\n    k_rot_r: EF,\n}\n```\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` (near `UnstackedSlice` definition, around line 29)\n\nAdd matching CUDA struct:\n\n```c\nstruct DegenerateWindowMeta {\n    uint32_t col_offset;\n    uint32_t eq_ub_offset;\n    uint32_t window_len;\n    uint32_t _pad;\n    FpExt eq_r;\n    FpExt k_rot_r;\n};\n```\n\nLayout: `[col_offset:4][eq_ub_offset:4][window_len:4][_pad:4][eq_r:16][k_rot_r:16]` = 48 bytes. The `_pad` field aligns the `FpExt` fields to 16-byte offsets, which is not strictly required for correctness (since `FpExt` has 4-byte natural alignment) but benefits GPU memory access patterns.\n\n### Step 2: Add batched CUDA kernel\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\nAdd new kernel (after the existing `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_kernel`, around line 368):\n\n```c\n// Batched degenerate case: one block per window, all atomically accumulate into shared output.\n__global__ void stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched_kernel(\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ const *__restrict__ q_evals,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_ub_all,\n    const UnstackedSlice *__restrict__ unstacked_cols_global,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ lambda_pows_global,\n    const DegenerateWindowMeta *__restrict__ metas,\n    uint64_t *__restrict__ output,\n    uint32_t q_height,\n    uint32_t shift_factor\n) {\n    extern __shared__ char smem[];\n    FpExt *shared = (FpExt *)smem;\n\n    // Each block handles one degenerate window\n    DegenerateWindowMeta meta = metas[blockIdx.x];\n    FpExt eq_r = meta.eq_r;\n    FpExt k_rot_r = meta.k_rot_r;\n    const UnstackedSlice *unstacked_cols = unstacked_cols_global + meta.col_offset;\n    const FpExt *lambda_pows = lambda_pows_global + 2 * meta.col_offset;\n    const FpExt *eq_ub_ptr = eq_ub_all + meta.eq_ub_offset;\n    uint32_t window_len = meta.window_len;\n\n    FpExt local_sums[S_DEG];\n#pragma unroll\n    for (int i = 0; i < S_DEG; i++) {\n        local_sums[i] = FpExt(0);\n    }\n\n    for (uint32_t window_idx = threadIdx.x; window_idx < window_len; window_idx += blockDim.x) {\n        UnstackedSlice s = unstacked_cols[window_idx];\n        const FpExt *__restrict__ q = q_evals[s.commit_idx];\n\n        auto col_idx = s.stacked_col_idx;\n        auto row_idx = s.stacked_row_idx;\n        auto row_start = (row_idx >> shift_factor) << 1;\n        auto q_offset = col_idx * q_height + row_start;\n\n        auto q_0 = q[q_offset];\n        auto q_1 = q[q_offset + 1];\n        auto q_c1 = q_1 - q_0;\n\n        uint32_t b_bool = (row_idx >> (shift_factor - 1)) & 1;\n        Fp b = Fp(b_bool);\n\n        auto eq_ub = eq_ub_ptr[window_idx];\n\n#pragma unroll\n        for (int x_int = 1; x_int <= S_DEG; ++x_int) {\n            Fp x = Fp(x_int);\n            auto eq_ub_x = eq_ub * eq1(x, b);\n            auto eq = eq_r * eq_ub_x;\n            auto k_rot = k_rot_r * eq_ub_x;\n\n            auto q_x = q_0 + q_c1 * x;\n\n            local_sums[x_int - 1] +=\n                (lambda_pows[2 * window_idx] * eq + lambda_pows[2 * window_idx + 1] * k_rot) * q_x;\n        }\n    }\n\n#pragma unroll\n    for (int idx = 0; idx < S_DEG; idx++) {\n        FpExt reduced = sumcheck::block_reduce_sum(local_sums[idx], shared);\n        if (threadIdx.x == 0) {\n            sumcheck::atomic_add_fpext_to_u64(output + idx * 4, reduced);\n        }\n        __syncthreads();\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe inner loop body is identical to the existing degenerate kernel. The only difference is:\n- `blockIdx.x` selects the window (instead of always being 0).\n- Per-window parameters (`eq_r`, `k_rot_r`, pointers) are loaded from the `metas` array instead of kernel arguments.\n\n### Step 3: Add batched launcher\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` (after the existing degenerate launcher, around line 570)\n\n```c\nextern \"C\" int _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n    const FpExt *const *q_evals,\n    const FpExt *eq_ub_all,\n    const UnstackedSlice *unstacked_cols,\n    const FpExt *lambda_pows,\n    const DegenerateWindowMeta *metas,\n    uint64_t *output,\n    uint32_t q_height,\n    uint32_t num_windows,\n    uint32_t shift_factor\n) {\n    dim3 block(256);\n    dim3 grid(num_windows);\n    // num_windows * 256 < 65535 * 256 < 2^24 << 2^64, no overflow risk\n    size_t shmem_bytes = div_ceil(block.x, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt);\n\n    stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched_kernel<<<grid, block, shmem_bytes>>>(\n        q_evals, eq_ub_all, unstacked_cols, lambda_pows, metas,\n        output, q_height, shift_factor\n    );\n\n    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n}\n```\n\nBlock size is fixed at 256. Windows with `window_len < 256` have idle threads that skip the inner loop — this is a minor inefficiency but eliminates the need for per-window block size tuning. The original kernel used `min(window_len, 256)`, so the worst case is launching 256 threads for a window with 1 column. At ~3.9us average GPU time per degenerate window, this inefficiency is negligible.\n\n### Step 4: Add Rust FFI binding\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n\nAdd extern declaration (inside the existing `extern \"C\"` block):\n\n```rust\nfn _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n    q_evals: *const *const EF,\n    eq_ub_all: *const EF,\n    unstacked_cols: *const UnstackedSlice,\n    lambda_pows: *const EF,\n    metas: *const DegenerateWindowMeta,\n    output: *mut u64,\n    q_height: u32,\n    num_windows: u32,\n    shift_factor: u32,\n) -> i32;\n```\n\nAdd safe wrapper function (after the existing `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate` wrapper):\n\n```rust\n/// Batched degenerate case: launches one block per degenerate window, all atomically\n/// accumulating into a single output buffer. The caller must zero-initialize `output`\n/// before calling.\n#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\npub unsafe fn stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n    q_evals: &DeviceBuffer<*const EF>,\n    eq_ub_all: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    unstacked_cols: &DeviceBuffer<UnstackedSlice>,\n    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    metas: &DeviceBuffer<DegenerateWindowMeta>,\n    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<u64>,\n    q_height: usize,\n    num_windows: usize,\n    l_skip: usize,\n    round: usize,\n) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n    debug_assert!(output.len() >= STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG * D_EF);\n    debug_assert!(num_windows <= 65535, \"num_windows exceeds max grid.x\");\n\n    check(_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n        q_evals.as_ptr(),\n        eq_ub_all.as_ptr(),\n        unstacked_cols.as_ptr(),\n        lambda_pows.as_ptr(),\n        metas.as_ptr(),\n        output.as_mut_ptr(),\n        q_height as u32,\n        num_windows as u32,\n        (l_skip + round) as u32,\n    ))\n}\n```\n\nImport `DegenerateWindowMeta` from the parent module. Add to the existing imports at the top of the file:\n\n```rust\nuse crate::stacked_reduction::{DegenerateWindowMeta, UnstackedSlice, STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG};\n```\n\n(Adjust the existing `use crate::stacked_reduction::...` import to include `DegenerateWindowMeta`.)\n\n### Step 5: Add error variant\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/error.rs`\n\nAdd new variant to `StackedReductionError` enum:\n\n```rust\n#[error(\"sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched: {0}\")]\nSumcheckMleRoundDegenerateBatched(CudaError),\n```\n\n### Step 6: Restructure `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval`\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, function `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (lines 793-912)\n\nReplace lines 832-911 (the per-window loop + final sum) with:\n\n```rust\n// Phase 1: Classify windows into degenerate vs non-degenerate\nlet mut degen_metas: Vec<DegenerateWindowMeta> = Vec::new();\nlet mut degen_eq_ub: Vec<EF> = Vec::new();\nlet mut non_degen_windows: Vec<[usize; 2]> = Vec::new();\n\nfor window in self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2) {\n    let window_start = window[0];\n    let window_end = window[1];\n    let window_len = window_end - window_start;\n    let log_height = self.unstacked_cols[window_start].log_height as usize;\n\n    if log_height < l_skip + round {\n        let eq_ub_offset = degen_eq_ub.len();\n        degen_eq_ub.extend_from_slice(&self.eq_ub_per_trace[window_start..window_end]);\n        degen_metas.push(DegenerateWindowMeta {\n            col_offset: window_start as u32,\n            eq_ub_offset: eq_ub_offset as u32,\n            window_len: window_len as u32,\n            _pad: 0,\n            eq_r: self.eq_stable[log_height],\n            k_rot_r: self.k_rot_stable[log_height],\n        });\n    } else {\n        non_degen_windows.push([window_start, window_end]);\n    }\n}\n\n// Phase 2: Batch launch all degenerate windows\nlet mut total_evals = [EF::ZERO; STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG];\n\nif !degen_metas.is_empty() {\n    self.d_accum\n        .fill_zero()\n        .map_err(StackedReductionError::FillZero)?;\n\n    // Upload metadata\n    let d_metas = degen_metas.to_device()?;\n\n    // Upload concatenated eq_ub values\n    if degen_eq_ub.len() > self.d_eq_ub.len() {\n        self.d_eq_ub = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(degen_eq_ub.len());\n    }\n    degen_eq_ub.copy_to(&mut self.d_eq_ub)?;\n\n    let stacked_height = self.stacked_height(round);\n    unsafe {\n        stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n            &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n            &self.d_eq_ub,\n            &self.d_unstacked_cols,\n            &self.d_lambda_pows,\n            &d_metas,\n            &mut self.d_accum,\n            stacked_height,\n            degen_metas.len(),\n            l_skip,\n            round,\n        )\n        .map_err(StackedReductionError::SumcheckMleRoundDegenerateBatched)?;\n    }\n\n    let h_accum = self.d_accum.to_host()?;\n    let degen_evals = reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(&h_accum);\n    for i in 0..STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG {\n        total_evals[i] += degen_evals[i];\n    }\n    // d_metas dropped here (stream-ordered free)\n}\n\n// Phase 3: Per-window non-degenerate launches (keep existing logic)\nfor &[window_start, window_end] in &non_degen_windows {\n    let window_len = window_end - window_start;\n    let unstacked_cols_ptr = unsafe { self.d_unstacked_cols.as_ptr().add(window_start) };\n    let lambda_pows_ptr = unsafe { self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr().add(2 * window_start) };\n    let log_height = self.unstacked_cols[window_start].log_height as usize;\n    let hypercube_dim = log_height - l_skip - round;\n    let num_y = 1 << hypercube_dim;\n\n    self.d_accum\n        .fill_zero()\n        .map_err(StackedReductionError::FillZero)?;\n\n    let stacked_height = self.stacked_height(round);\n    unsafe {\n        stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round(\n            &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n            &self.eq_r_ns,\n            &self.k_rot_ns,\n            unstacked_cols_ptr,\n            lambda_pows_ptr,\n            &mut self.d_accum,\n            stacked_height,\n            window_len,\n            num_y,\n            self.sm_count,\n        )\n        .map_err(StackedReductionError::SumcheckMleRound)?;\n    };\n\n    let h_accum = self.d_accum.to_host()?;\n    let evals = reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(&h_accum);\n    for i in 0..STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG {\n        total_evals[i] += evals[i];\n    }\n}\n\nOk(total_evals)\n```\n\nAdd to the imports at the top of `stacked_reduction.rs`:\n\n```rust\nuse crate::cuda::stacked_reduction::stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched;\n```\n\nThe existing import of `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate` (line 34) is no longer needed and can be removed. The existing import of `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round` (line 33) is kept for non-degenerate windows.\n\n### Summary of Touched Files\n\n| File | What changes |\n|---|---|\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs:~150` | Add `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs:832-911` | Replace per-window loop with classification + batched degenerate + per-window non-degenerate |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (imports) | Add batched launcher import, remove unused degenerate import |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu:~29` | Add `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu:~368` | Add batched degenerate kernel |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu:~570` | Add batched degenerate launcher |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs` | Add FFI extern declaration + safe wrapper for batched launcher |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/error.rs` | Add `SumcheckMleRoundDegenerateBatched` variant |\n\nNo other files are modified. The old per-window degenerate kernel and launcher remain in the codebase (dead code) — they can be removed in a follow-up cleanup if the batched version is proven correct.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Output equivalence**: The function returns `[EF; STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG]` computed as the sum over all windows' contributions. In the current code, each window atomically accumulates into `d_accum`, which is read back and summed on CPU. In the new code, all degenerate windows atomically accumulate into the same `d_accum` in one kernel launch, and non-degenerate windows still get their own per-window cycle. Since addition is commutative and associative over EF, the final sum is identical regardless of accumulation order.\n\n2. **Atomic accumulation correctness**: The batched kernel uses the same `atomic_add_fpext_to_u64` as the existing degenerate kernel. Multiple blocks writing to the same output is safe because:\n   - Atomic operations are sequentially consistent on NVIDIA GPUs.\n   - The u64 accumulators cannot overflow: 10,348 blocks x 256 threads x ~2^31 max per component < 2^45 << 2^64.\n   - The `d_accum` buffer is zero-initialized once before the batched launch.\n\n3. **Memory safety**:\n   - `d_metas` is a temporary `DeviceBuffer` created by `to_device()`, lives until dropped after the D2H copy. All kernel accesses complete before the drop because `to_host()` synchronizes the stream.\n   - `d_eq_ub` is resized if needed to hold all degenerate eq_ub values. The resize drops the old buffer (stream-ordered free) and allocates a new one. This is safe because the old buffer is not in use.\n   - `d_unstacked_cols` and `d_lambda_pows` are persistent fields, valid for the lifetime of `StackedReductionGpu`.\n\n4. **Kernel computation correctness**: The batched kernel's inner loop body is character-for-character identical to the existing degenerate kernel. Per-window parameters (`eq_r`, `k_rot_r`, pointers, `window_len`) are loaded from the metadata array instead of kernel arguments, but the values are the same.\n\n5. **Non-degenerate path unchanged**: The non-degenerate windows use the exact same code as before (same kernel, same fill_zero/to_host cycle, same auto-tuning). The only change is the loop iteration source (a pre-classified `Vec<[usize; 2]>` instead of inline classification).\n\n6. **Round progression correctness**: `eq_stable` and `k_rot_stable` are updated at the start of `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (lines 804-831, unchanged). The classification loop reads from these updated values, so each round uses the correct scalars.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n### Before (baseline for this task)\n\nRun the pairing benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 on the current code (after the previous Round 0 optimization):\n\n```bash\ncd /path/to/powdr\nopenvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh  # for each APC config\n```\n\nCollect `metrics.json` for each config. Analyze with:\n\n```bash\npython spec.py results/pairing/<config>/metrics.json before_<config>\n```\n\nRecord \"Stacked Reduction\" and \"STARK (excl. trace)\" values.\n\n### After\n\nApply the changes, then rerun the same benchmarks:\n\n```bash\ncd /path/to/powdr\nopenvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh  # for each APC config\n```\n\nCollect new `metrics.json` files. Analyze with:\n\n```bash\npython spec.py results/pairing/<config>/metrics.json after_<config>\n```\n\n### What to Compare\n\n| Metric | APC 0 | APC 100 | APC 300 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Stacked Reduction (ms) | before vs after | before vs after | before vs after |\n| STARK excl trace (ms) | before vs after | before vs after | before vs after |\n| Ratio APC300/APC0 STARK excl trace | before vs after | | |\n\n### Correctness Verification\n\n```bash\ncargo nextest run -p openvm-cuda-backend --test-threads=4\n```\n\nAll existing tests must pass. The pairing benchmark itself also verifies proof correctness.\n\n### GPU Memory Check\n\nMonitor physical GPU memory during the APC 300 run using `nvidia-smi` to verify no significant peak memory increase. The per-round metadata upload is ~10K * 48 bytes = ~480KB (plus eq_ub), negligible relative to GPU memory budget.\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n1. **Correctness failure**: Any test failure or proof verification failure -> immediate revert.\n2. **Insufficient improvement**: If Stacked Reduction APC 300 improves by less than 100ms (< 32% of ~310ms), the optimization is not delivering expected value -> revert.\n3. **Regression on APC 0**: If APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 20ms -> investigate before committing.\n4. **GPU memory regression**: If physical peak GPU memory (from `nvidia-smi`) increases by more than 100MB -> investigate. Per-round metadata is <1MB so this should not happen.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":262,"cache_read_input_tokens":81952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":262},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f75a9bb0-08dc-4cc2-8653-93cb45f6f821","uuid":"def8c412-af7f-4563-9ff0-fb7e427f480a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UfxjbA9ssShTvoSmfAFmMF","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-10-2145-batch-degenerate-stacked-reduction/plan.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f75a9bb0-08dc-4cc2-8653-93cb45f6f821","uuid":"864936fb-4c4b-4eae-9312-aca9e09a1862","timestamp":"2026-04-10T18:16:34.491Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-10-2145-batch-degenerate-stacked-reduction/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Batch Degenerate Stacked Reduction Kernel Launches\n\n## Goal\n\nBatch all degenerate-window kernel launches within `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` into a single GPU kernel launch per round, eliminating ~10,348 tiny kernel launches (at APC 300) that contribute ~217ms of CPU-side launch/sync overhead. The degenerate case handles windows where `log_height < l_skip + round`, producing single-block kernels with `grid(1)`. Because all window results are summed at the end (line 909-911), they can be atomically accumulated into one shared output buffer by a single multi-block launch.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Call Chain\n\n1. `prove_stacked_opening_reduction_gpu` (`stacked_reduction.rs:185`) calls `prover.batch_sumcheck_poly_eval(round, u_prev)` for each MLE round 1..=n_stack (line 244).\n2. `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (`stacked_reduction.rs:793-912`):\n   - Lines 800-802: Collect `q_eval_ptrs` and upload to device.\n   - Lines 804-831: If applicable, D2H copy stable `eq_r` and `k_rot_r` values for the current round.\n   - Lines 832-907: **The per-window loop** (this is what we modify).\n   - Lines 909-911: Sum all per-window results: `s_evals_batch.iter().map(|evals| evals[i]).sum()`.\n\n### The Per-Window Loop (lines 832-907)\n\nFor each window in `ht_diff_idxs.windows(2)`:\n\n1. Compute `unstacked_cols_ptr` and `lambda_pows_ptr` from window offset (lines 836-839).\n2. Get `log_height` from first column in window (line 841).\n3. `d_accum.fill_zero()` — memset kernel (line 844-846).\n4. **Branch on degenerate condition** (`log_height < l_skip + round`):\n   - **Degenerate path** (lines 848-878):\n     - Get `eq_r = eq_stable[log_height]`, `k_rot_r = k_rot_stable[log_height]` (scalars, on host).\n     - H2D copy: `eq_ub_per_trace[window_start..window_end]` -> `d_eq_ub` (line 861).\n     - Kernel launch: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate(...)` with `grid(1), block(min(window_len, 256))` (line 864).\n   - **Non-degenerate path** (lines 879-901):\n     - Compute `num_y = 1 << (log_height - l_skip - round)`.\n     - Kernel launch: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round(...)` with auto-tuned grid.\n5. `d_accum.to_host()` — D2H copy + implicit sync via `cudaEventSynchronize` (line 904).\n6. `reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(&h_accum)` — reduce u64 accumulators modulo P (line 905).\n7. Push per-window result to `s_evals_batch` (line 906).\n\n### Why It's Slow\n\nEach degenerate window iteration involves 4 CUDA runtime API calls:\n1. `fill_zero()` -> `cudaMemsetAsync` (memset kernel)\n2. `copy_to()` -> `cudaMemcpyAsync` (H2D for eq_ub slice)\n3. Kernel launch -> `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_kernel<<<grid(1), block(...)>>>`\n4. `to_host()` -> `cudaMemcpyAsync` (D2H) + `cudaEventSynchronize` (blocking sync)\n\nAt APC 300, there are ~10,348 degenerate windows per round. Nsight profiling shows GPU kernel time is ~93ms but wall-clock is 310ms. The ~217ms gap (70%) is CPU-side CUDA runtime overhead from issuing and synchronizing 10,348+ tiny operations sequentially.\n\n### Key Properties\n\n- **All window results are summed**: `from_fn(|i| s_evals_batch.iter().map(|evals| evals[i]).sum())` (line 909-911). This means all degenerate contributions can be accumulated into a single output buffer via atomics.\n- **Windows are independent**: No data dependencies between windows. Each reads from its own slice of `unstacked_cols`, `lambda_pows`, and `eq_ub_per_trace`.\n- **Existing kernel already uses atomics**: The degenerate kernel calls `sumcheck::atomic_add_fpext_to_u64(output + idx * 4, reduced)` (stacked_reduction.cu:364). Multiple blocks writing to the same output is safe.\n- **Overflow is not a risk**: 10,348 blocks x max 256 threads x ~2^31 per component < 2^45 << 2^64.\n- **`unstacked_cols` and `lambda_pows` are already on device**: `d_unstacked_cols` and `d_lambda_pows` are uploaded once in `StackedReductionGpu::new()` (lines 393, 391). We only need to pass per-window offsets.\n- **`eq_ub_per_trace` is on host only**: Must be gathered and uploaded for degenerate windows.\n- **`FpExt`/`bb31_4_t` has 4-byte natural alignment**: `__align__(16)` was explicitly removed from `bb31_4_t` (see `crates/cuda-common/include/ff/baby_bear.hpp:75`). This means `#[repr(C)]` structs containing `FpExt` fields will pack identically on both Rust and CUDA sides without hidden padding.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Overview\n\nSplit the per-window loop into:\n1. **Classification**: Separate degenerate vs non-degenerate windows.\n2. **Batched degenerate path**: One `fill_zero` + one H2D + one kernel launch + one D2H for all degenerate windows.\n3. **Per-window non-degenerate path**: Keep existing logic (these already have auto-tuned multi-block launches with meaningful GPU work).\n\n### Step 1: Define `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (near `UnstackedSlice` definition, around line 150)\n\nAdd a new FFI-compatible struct:\n\n```rust\n/// Per-window metadata for the batched degenerate kernel.\n/// Must match the CUDA-side `DegenerateWindowMeta` layout exactly.\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\npub(crate) struct DegenerateWindowMeta {\n    /// Offset into the global `d_unstacked_cols` / `d_lambda_pows` arrays.\n    col_offset: u32,\n    /// Offset into the concatenated `d_eq_ub` buffer for this window's eq_ub values.\n    eq_ub_offset: u32,\n    /// Number of columns in this window.\n    window_len: u32,\n    /// Padding for alignment (keeps FpExt fields at 16-byte boundary).\n    _pad: u32,\n    /// Folded eq evaluation for this window's log_height: `eq_stable[log_height]`.\n    eq_r: EF,\n    /// Folded k_rot evaluation for this window's log_height: `k_rot_stable[log_height]`.\n    k_rot_r: EF,\n}\n```\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` (near `UnstackedSlice` definition, around line 29)\n\nAdd matching CUDA struct:\n\n```c\nstruct DegenerateWindowMeta {\n    uint32_t col_offset;\n    uint32_t eq_ub_offset;\n    uint32_t window_len;\n    uint32_t _pad;\n    FpExt eq_r;\n    FpExt k_rot_r;\n};\n```\n\nLayout: `[col_offset:4][eq_ub_offset:4][window_len:4][_pad:4][eq_r:16][k_rot_r:16]` = 48 bytes. The `_pad` field aligns the `FpExt` fields to 16-byte offsets, which is not strictly required for correctness (since `FpExt` has 4-byte natural alignment) but benefits GPU memory access patterns.\n\n### Step 2: Add batched CUDA kernel\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\nAdd new kernel (after the existing `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_kernel`, around line 368):\n\n```c\n// Batched degenerate case: one block per window, all atomically accumulate into shared output.\n__global__ void stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched_kernel(\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ const *__restrict__ q_evals,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_ub_all,\n    const UnstackedSlice *__restrict__ unstacked_cols_global,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ lambda_pows_global,\n    const DegenerateWindowMeta *__restrict__ metas,\n    uint64_t *__restrict__ output,\n    uint32_t q_height,\n    uint32_t shift_factor\n) {\n    extern __shared__ char smem[];\n    FpExt *shared = (FpExt *)smem;\n\n    // Each block handles one degenerate window\n    DegenerateWindowMeta meta = metas[blockIdx.x];\n    FpExt eq_r = meta.eq_r;\n    FpExt k_rot_r = meta.k_rot_r;\n    const UnstackedSlice *unstacked_cols = unstacked_cols_global + meta.col_offset;\n    const FpExt *lambda_pows = lambda_pows_global + 2 * meta.col_offset;\n    const FpExt *eq_ub_ptr = eq_ub_all + meta.eq_ub_offset;\n    uint32_t window_len = meta.window_len;\n\n    FpExt local_sums[S_DEG];\n#pragma unroll\n    for (int i = 0; i < S_DEG; i++) {\n        local_sums[i] = FpExt(0);\n    }\n\n    for (uint32_t window_idx = threadIdx.x; window_idx < window_len; window_idx += blockDim.x) {\n        UnstackedSlice s = unstacked_cols[window_idx];\n        const FpExt *__restrict__ q = q_evals[s.commit_idx];\n\n        auto col_idx = s.stacked_col_idx;\n        auto row_idx = s.stacked_row_idx;\n        auto row_start = (row_idx >> shift_factor) << 1;\n        auto q_offset = col_idx * q_height + row_start;\n\n        auto q_0 = q[q_offset];\n        auto q_1 = q[q_offset + 1];\n        auto q_c1 = q_1 - q_0;\n\n        uint32_t b_bool = (row_idx >> (shift_factor - 1)) & 1;\n        Fp b = Fp(b_bool);\n\n        auto eq_ub = eq_ub_ptr[window_idx];\n\n#pragma unroll\n        for (int x_int = 1; x_int <= S_DEG; ++x_int) {\n            Fp x = Fp(x_int);\n            auto eq_ub_x = eq_ub * eq1(x, b);\n            auto eq = eq_r * eq_ub_x;\n            auto k_rot = k_rot_r * eq_ub_x;\n\n            auto q_x = q_0 + q_c1 * x;\n\n            local_sums[x_int - 1] +=\n                (lambda_pows[2 * window_idx] * eq + lambda_pows[2 * window_idx + 1] * k_rot) * q_x;\n        }\n    }\n\n#pragma unroll\n    for (int idx = 0; idx < S_DEG; idx++) {\n        FpExt reduced = sumcheck::block_reduce_sum(local_sums[idx], shared);\n        if (threadIdx.x == 0) {\n            sumcheck::atomic_add_fpext_to_u64(output + idx * 4, reduced);\n        }\n        __syncthreads();\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe inner loop body is identical to the existing degenerate kernel. The only difference is:\n- `blockIdx.x` selects the window (instead of always being 0).\n- Per-window parameters (`eq_r`, `k_rot_r`, pointers) are loaded from the `metas` array instead of kernel arguments.\n\n### Step 3: Add batched launcher\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` (after the existing degenerate launcher, around line 570)\n\n```c\nextern \"C\" int _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n    const FpExt *const *q_evals,\n    const FpExt *eq_ub_all,\n    const UnstackedSlice *unstacked_cols,\n    const FpExt *lambda_pows,\n    const DegenerateWindowMeta *metas,\n    uint64_t *output,\n    uint32_t q_height,\n    uint32_t num_windows,\n    uint32_t shift_factor\n) {\n    dim3 block(256);\n    dim3 grid(num_windows);\n    // num_windows * 256 < 65535 * 256 < 2^24 << 2^64, no overflow risk\n    size_t shmem_bytes = div_ceil(block.x, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt);\n\n    stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched_kernel<<<grid, block, shmem_bytes>>>(\n        q_evals, eq_ub_all, unstacked_cols, lambda_pows, metas,\n        output, q_height, shift_factor\n    );\n\n    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n}\n```\n\nBlock size is fixed at 256. Windows with `window_len < 256` have idle threads that skip the inner loop — this is a minor inefficiency but eliminates the need for per-window block size tuning. The original kernel used `min(window_len, 256)`, so the worst case is launching 256 threads for a window with 1 column. At ~3.9us average GPU time per degenerate window, this inefficiency is negligible.\n\n### Step 4: Add Rust FFI binding\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n\nAdd extern declaration (inside the existing `extern \"C\"` block):\n\n```rust\nfn _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n    q_evals: *const *const EF,\n    eq_ub_all: *const EF,\n    unstacked_cols: *const UnstackedSlice,\n    lambda_pows: *const EF,\n    metas: *const DegenerateWindowMeta,\n    output: *mut u64,\n    q_height: u32,\n    num_windows: u32,\n    shift_factor: u32,\n) -> i32;\n```\n\nAdd safe wrapper function (after the existing `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate` wrapper):\n\n```rust\n/// Batched degenerate case: launches one block per degenerate window, all atomically\n/// accumulating into a single output buffer. The caller must zero-initialize `output`\n/// before calling.\n#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\npub unsafe fn stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n    q_evals: &DeviceBuffer<*const EF>,\n    eq_ub_all: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    unstacked_cols: &DeviceBuffer<UnstackedSlice>,\n    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    metas: &DeviceBuffer<DegenerateWindowMeta>,\n    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<u64>,\n    q_height: usize,\n    num_windows: usize,\n    l_skip: usize,\n    round: usize,\n) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n    debug_assert!(output.len() >= STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG * D_EF);\n    debug_assert!(num_windows <= 65535, \"num_windows exceeds max grid.x\");\n\n    check(_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n        q_evals.as_ptr(),\n        eq_ub_all.as_ptr(),\n        unstacked_cols.as_ptr(),\n        lambda_pows.as_ptr(),\n        metas.as_ptr(),\n        output.as_mut_ptr(),\n        q_height as u32,\n        num_windows as u32,\n        (l_skip + round) as u32,\n    ))\n}\n```\n\nImport `DegenerateWindowMeta` from the parent module. Add to the existing imports at the top of the file:\n\n```rust\nuse crate::stacked_reduction::{DegenerateWindowMeta, UnstackedSlice, STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG};\n```\n\n(Adjust the existing `use crate::stacked_reduction::...` import to include `DegenerateWindowMeta`.)\n\n### Step 5: Add error variant\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/error.rs`\n\nAdd new variant to `StackedReductionError` enum:\n\n```rust\n#[error(\"sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched: {0}\")]\nSumcheckMleRoundDegenerateBatched(CudaError),\n```\n\n### Step 6: Restructure `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval`\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, function `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (lines 793-912)\n\nReplace lines 832-911 (the per-window loop + final sum) with:\n\n```rust\n// Phase 1: Classify windows into degenerate vs non-degenerate\nlet mut degen_metas: Vec<DegenerateWindowMeta> = Vec::new();\nlet mut degen_eq_ub: Vec<EF> = Vec::new();\nlet mut non_degen_windows: Vec<[usize; 2]> = Vec::new();\n\nfor window in self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2) {\n    let window_start = window[0];\n    let window_end = window[1];\n    let window_len = window_end - window_start;\n    let log_height = self.unstacked_cols[window_start].log_height as usize;\n\n    if log_height < l_skip + round {\n        let eq_ub_offset = degen_eq_ub.len();\n        degen_eq_ub.extend_from_slice(&self.eq_ub_per_trace[window_start..window_end]);\n        degen_metas.push(DegenerateWindowMeta {\n            col_offset: window_start as u32,\n            eq_ub_offset: eq_ub_offset as u32,\n            window_len: window_len as u32,\n            _pad: 0,\n            eq_r: self.eq_stable[log_height],\n            k_rot_r: self.k_rot_stable[log_height],\n        });\n    } else {\n        non_degen_windows.push([window_start, window_end]);\n    }\n}\n\n// Phase 2: Batch launch all degenerate windows\nlet mut total_evals = [EF::ZERO; STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG];\n\nif !degen_metas.is_empty() {\n    self.d_accum\n        .fill_zero()\n        .map_err(StackedReductionError::FillZero)?;\n\n    // Upload metadata\n    let d_metas = degen_metas.to_device()?;\n\n    // Upload concatenated eq_ub values\n    if degen_eq_ub.len() > self.d_eq_ub.len() {\n        self.d_eq_ub = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(degen_eq_ub.len());\n    }\n    degen_eq_ub.copy_to(&mut self.d_eq_ub)?;\n\n    let stacked_height = self.stacked_height(round);\n    unsafe {\n        stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n            &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n            &self.d_eq_ub,\n            &self.d_unstacked_cols,\n            &self.d_lambda_pows,\n            &d_metas,\n            &mut self.d_accum,\n            stacked_height,\n            degen_metas.len(),\n            l_skip,\n            round,\n        )\n        .map_err(StackedReductionError::SumcheckMleRoundDegenerateBatched)?;\n    }\n\n    let h_accum = self.d_accum.to_host()?;\n    let degen_evals = reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(&h_accum);\n    for i in 0..STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG {\n        total_evals[i] += degen_evals[i];\n    }\n    // d_metas dropped here (stream-ordered free)\n}\n\n// Phase 3: Per-window non-degenerate launches (keep existing logic)\nfor &[window_start, window_end] in &non_degen_windows {\n    let window_len = window_end - window_start;\n    let unstacked_cols_ptr = unsafe { self.d_unstacked_cols.as_ptr().add(window_start) };\n    let lambda_pows_ptr = unsafe { self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr().add(2 * window_start) };\n    let log_height = self.unstacked_cols[window_start].log_height as usize;\n    let hypercube_dim = log_height - l_skip - round;\n    let num_y = 1 << hypercube_dim;\n\n    self.d_accum\n        .fill_zero()\n        .map_err(StackedReductionError::FillZero)?;\n\n    let stacked_height = self.stacked_height(round);\n    unsafe {\n        stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round(\n            &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n            &self.eq_r_ns,\n            &self.k_rot_ns,\n            unstacked_cols_ptr,\n            lambda_pows_ptr,\n            &mut self.d_accum,\n            stacked_height,\n            window_len,\n            num_y,\n            self.sm_count,\n        )\n        .map_err(StackedReductionError::SumcheckMleRound)?;\n    };\n\n    let h_accum = self.d_accum.to_host()?;\n    let evals = reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(&h_accum);\n    for i in 0..STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG {\n        total_evals[i] += evals[i];\n    }\n}\n\nOk(total_evals)\n```\n\nAdd to the imports at the top of `stacked_reduction.rs`:\n\n```rust\nuse crate::cuda::stacked_reduction::stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched;\n```\n\nThe existing import of `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate` (line 34) is no longer needed and can be removed. The existing import of `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round` (line 33) is kept for non-degenerate windows.\n\n### Summary of Touched Files\n\n| File | What changes |\n|---|---|\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs:~150` | Add `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs:832-911` | Replace per-window loop with classification + batched degenerate + per-window non-degenerate |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (imports) | Add batched launcher import, remove unused degenerate import |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu:~29` | Add `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu:~368` | Add batched degenerate kernel |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu:~570` | Add batched degenerate launcher |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs` | Add FFI extern declaration + safe wrapper for batched launcher |\n| `crates/cuda-backend/src/error.rs` | Add `SumcheckMleRoundDegenerateBatched` variant |\n\nNo other files are modified. The old per-window degenerate kernel and launcher remain in the codebase (dead code) — they can be removed in a follow-up cleanup if the batched version is proven correct.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Output equivalence**: The function returns `[EF; STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG]` computed as the sum over all windows' contributions. In the current code, each window atomically accumulates into `d_accum`, which is read back and summed on CPU. In the new code, all degenerate windows atomically accumulate into the same `d_accum` in one kernel launch, and non-degenerate windows still get their own per-window cycle. Since addition is commutative and associative over EF, the final sum is identical regardless of accumulation order.\n\n2. **Atomic accumulation correctness**: The batched kernel uses the same `atomic_add_fpext_to_u64` as the existing degenerate kernel. Multiple blocks writing to the same output is safe because:\n   - Atomic operations are sequentially consistent on NVIDIA GPUs.\n   - The u64 accumulators cannot overflow: 10,348 blocks x 256 threads x ~2^31 max per component < 2^45 << 2^64.\n   - The `d_accum` buffer is zero-initialized once before the batched launch.\n\n3. **Memory safety**:\n   - `d_metas` is a temporary `DeviceBuffer` created by `to_device()`, lives until dropped after the D2H copy. All kernel accesses complete before the drop because `to_host()` synchronizes the stream.\n   - `d_eq_ub` is resized if needed to hold all degenerate eq_ub values. The resize drops the old buffer (stream-ordered free) and allocates a new one. This is safe because the old buffer is not in use.\n   - `d_unstacked_cols` and `d_lambda_pows` are persistent fields, valid for the lifetime of `StackedReductionGpu`.\n\n4. **Kernel computation correctness**: The batched kernel's inner loop body is character-for-character identical to the existing degenerate kernel. Per-window parameters (`eq_r`, `k_rot_r`, pointers, `window_len`) are loaded from the metadata array instead of kernel arguments, but the values are the same.\n\n5. **Non-degenerate path unchanged**: The non-degenerate windows use the exact same code as before (same kernel, same fill_zero/to_host cycle, same auto-tuning). The only change is the loop iteration source (a pre-classified `Vec<[usize; 2]>` instead of inline classification).\n\n6. **Round progression correctness**: `eq_stable` and `k_rot_stable` are updated at the start of `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (lines 804-831, unchanged). The classification loop reads from these updated values, so each round uses the correct scalars.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n### Before (baseline for this task)\n\nRun the pairing benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 on the current code (after the previous Round 0 optimization):\n\n```bash\ncd /path/to/powdr\nopenvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh  # for each APC config\n```\n\nCollect `metrics.json` for each config. Analyze with:\n\n```bash\npython spec.py results/pairing/<config>/metrics.json before_<config>\n```\n\nRecord \"Stacked Reduction\" and \"STARK (excl. trace)\" values.\n\n### After\n\nApply the changes, then rerun the same benchmarks:\n\n```bash\ncd /path/to/powdr\nopenvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh  # for each APC config\n```\n\nCollect new `metrics.json` files. Analyze with:\n\n```bash\npython spec.py results/pairing/<config>/metrics.json after_<config>\n```\n\n### What to Compare\n\n| Metric | APC 0 | APC 100 | APC 300 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Stacked Reduction (ms) | before vs after | before vs after | before vs after |\n| STARK excl trace (ms) | before vs after | before vs after | before vs after |\n| Ratio APC300/APC0 STARK excl trace | before vs after | | |\n\n### Correctness Verification\n\n```bash\ncargo nextest run -p openvm-cuda-backend --test-threads=4\n```\n\nAll existing tests must pass. The pairing benchmark itself also verifies proof correctness.\n\n### GPU Memory Check\n\nMonitor physical GPU memory during the APC 300 run using `nvidia-smi` to verify no significant peak memory increase. The per-round metadata upload is ~10K * 48 bytes = ~480KB (plus eq_ub), negligible relative to GPU memory budget.\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n1. **Correctness failure**: Any test failure or proof verification failure -> immediate revert.\n2. **Insufficient improvement**: If Stacked Reduction APC 300 improves by less than 100ms (< 32% of ~310ms), the optimization is not delivering expected value -> revert.\n3. **Regression on APC 0**: If APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 20ms -> investigate before committing.\n4. **GPU memory regression**: If physical peak GPU memory (from `nvidia-smi`) increases by more than 100MB -> investigate. Per-round metadata is <1MB so this should not happen.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
