{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DZQ63tXz31DEu5zhU1Bk8u","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Batch Degenerate Stacked Reduction Kernel Launches\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tBatch all degenerate-window kernel launches within `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval()` into a single GPU kernel launch per round, eliminating ~10,348 tiny kernel launches (at APC 300) that contribute ~217ms of CPU-side launch/sync overhead. The degenerate case handles windows where `log_height < l_skip + round`, producing single-block kernels with `grid(1)`. Because all window results are summed at the end (line 909-911), they can be atomically accumulated into one shared output buffer by a single multi-block launch.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Call Chain\n10\t\n11\t1. `prove_stacked_opening_reduction_gpu` (`stacked_reduction.rs:185`) calls `prover.batch_sumcheck_poly_eval(round, u_prev)` for each MLE round 1..=n_stack (line 244).\n12\t2. `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (`stacked_reduction.rs:793-912`):\n13\t   - Lines 800-802: Collect `q_eval_ptrs` and upload to device.\n14\t   - Lines 804-831: If applicable, D2H copy stable `eq_r` and `k_rot_r` values for the current round.\n15\t   - Lines 832-907: **The per-window loop** (this is what we modify).\n16\t   - Lines 909-911: Sum all per-window results: `s_evals_batch.iter().map(|evals| evals[i]).sum()`.\n17\t\n18\t### The Per-Window Loop (lines 832-907)\n19\t\n20\tFor each window in `ht_diff_idxs.windows(2)`:\n21\t\n22\t1. Compute `unstacked_cols_ptr` and `lambda_pows_ptr` from window offset (lines 836-839).\n23\t2. Get `log_height` from first column in window (line 841).\n24\t3. `d_accum.fill_zero()` — memset kernel (line 844-846).\n25\t4. **Branch on degenerate condition** (`log_height < l_skip + round`):\n26\t   - **Degenerate path** (lines 848-878):\n27\t     - Get `eq_r = eq_stable[log_height]`, `k_rot_r = k_rot_stable[log_height]` (scalars, on host).\n28\t     - H2D copy: `eq_ub_per_trace[window_start..window_end]` -> `d_eq_ub` (line 861).\n29\t     - Kernel launch: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate(...)` with `grid(1), block(min(window_len, 256))` (line 864).\n30\t   - **Non-degenerate path** (lines 879-901):\n31\t     - Compute `num_y = 1 << (log_height - l_skip - round)`.\n32\t     - Kernel launch: `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round(...)` with auto-tuned grid.\n33\t5. `d_accum.to_host()` — D2H copy + implicit sync via `cudaEventSynchronize` (line 904).\n34\t6. `reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(&h_accum)` — reduce u64 accumulators modulo P (line 905).\n35\t7. Push per-window result to `s_evals_batch` (line 906).\n36\t\n37\t### Why It's Slow\n38\t\n39\tEach degenerate window iteration involves 4 CUDA runtime API calls:\n40\t1. `fill_zero()` -> `cudaMemsetAsync` (memset kernel)\n41\t2. `copy_to()` -> `cudaMemcpyAsync` (H2D for eq_ub slice)\n42\t3. Kernel launch -> `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_kernel<<<grid(1), block(...)>>>`\n43\t4. `to_host()` -> `cudaMemcpyAsync` (D2H) + `cudaEventSynchronize` (blocking sync)\n44\t\n45\tAt APC 300, there are ~10,348 degenerate windows per round. Nsight profiling shows GPU kernel time is ~93ms but wall-clock is 310ms. The ~217ms gap (70%) is CPU-side CUDA runtime overhead from issuing and synchronizing 10,348+ tiny operations sequentially.\n46\t\n47\t### Key Properties\n48\t\n49\t- **All window results are summed**: `from_fn(|i| s_evals_batch.iter().map(|evals| evals[i]).sum())` (line 909-911). This means all degenerate contributions can be accumulated into a single output buffer via atomics.\n50\t- **Windows are independent**: No data dependencies between windows. Each reads from its own slice of `unstacked_cols`, `lambda_pows`, and `eq_ub_per_trace`.\n51\t- **Existing kernel already uses atomics**: The degenerate kernel calls `sumcheck::atomic_add_fpext_to_u64(output + idx * 4, reduced)` (stacked_reduction.cu:364). Multiple blocks writing to the same output is safe.\n52\t- **Overflow is not a risk**: 10,348 blocks x max 256 threads x ~2^31 per component < 2^45 << 2^64.\n53\t- **`unstacked_cols` and `lambda_pows` are already on device**: `d_unstacked_cols` and `d_lambda_pows` are uploaded once in `StackedReductionGpu::new()` (lines 393, 391). We only need to pass per-window offsets.\n54\t- **`eq_ub_per_trace` is on host only**: Must be gathered and uploaded for degenerate windows.\n55\t- **`FpExt`/`bb31_4_t` has 4-byte natural alignment**: `__align__(16)` was explicitly removed from `bb31_4_t` (see `crates/cuda-common/include/ff/baby_bear.hpp:75`). This means `#[repr(C)]` structs containing `FpExt` fields will pack identically on both Rust and CUDA sides without hidden padding.\n56\t\n57\t## Changes\n58\t\n59\t### Overview\n60\t\n61\tSplit the per-window loop into:\n62\t1. **Classification**: Separate degenerate vs non-degenerate windows.\n63\t2. **Batched degenerate path**: One `fill_zero` + one H2D + one kernel launch + one D2H for all degenerate windows.\n64\t3. **Per-window non-degenerate path**: Keep existing logic (these already have auto-tuned multi-block launches with meaningful GPU work).\n65\t\n66\t### Step 1: Define `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct\n67\t\n68\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (near `UnstackedSlice` definition, around line 150)\n69\t\n70\tAdd a new FFI-compatible struct:\n71\t\n72\t```rust\n73\t/// Per-window metadata for the batched degenerate kernel.\n74\t/// Must match the CUDA-side `DegenerateWindowMeta` layout exactly.\n75\t#[repr(C)]\n76\t#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\n77\tpub(crate) struct DegenerateWindowMeta {\n78\t    /// Offset into the global `d_unstacked_cols` / `d_lambda_pows` arrays.\n79\t    col_offset: u32,\n80\t    /// Offset into the concatenated `d_eq_ub` buffer for this window's eq_ub values.\n81\t    eq_ub_offset: u32,\n82\t    /// Number of columns in this window.\n83\t    window_len: u32,\n84\t    /// Padding for alignment (keeps FpExt fields at 16-byte boundary).\n85\t    _pad: u32,\n86\t    /// Folded eq evaluation for this window's log_height: `eq_stable[log_height]`.\n87\t    eq_r: EF,\n88\t    /// Folded k_rot evaluation for this window's log_height: `k_rot_stable[log_height]`.\n89\t    k_rot_r: EF,\n90\t}\n91\t```\n92\t\n93\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` (near `UnstackedSlice` definition, around line 29)\n94\t\n95\tAdd matching CUDA struct:\n96\t\n97\t```c\n98\tstruct DegenerateWindowMeta {\n99\t    uint32_t col_offset;\n100\t    uint32_t eq_ub_offset;\n101\t    uint32_t window_len;\n102\t    uint32_t _pad;\n103\t    FpExt eq_r;\n104\t    FpExt k_rot_r;\n105\t};\n106\t```\n107\t\n108\tLayout: `[col_offset:4][eq_ub_offset:4][window_len:4][_pad:4][eq_r:16][k_rot_r:16]` = 48 bytes. The `_pad` field aligns the `FpExt` fields to 16-byte offsets, which is not strictly required for correctness (since `FpExt` has 4-byte natural alignment) but benefits GPU memory access patterns.\n109\t\n110\t### Step 2: Add batched CUDA kernel\n111\t\n112\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n113\t\n114\tAdd new kernel (after the existing `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_kernel`, around line 368):\n115\t\n116\t```c\n117\t// Batched degenerate case: one block per window, all atomically accumulate into shared output.\n118\t__global__ void stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched_kernel(\n119\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ const *__restrict__ q_evals,\n120\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_ub_all,\n121\t    const UnstackedSlice *__restrict__ unstacked_cols_global,\n122\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ lambda_pows_global,\n123\t    const DegenerateWindowMeta *__restrict__ metas,\n124\t    uint64_t *__restrict__ output,\n125\t    uint32_t q_height,\n126\t    uint32_t shift_factor\n127\t) {\n128\t    extern __shared__ char smem[];\n129\t    FpExt *shared = (FpExt *)smem;\n130\t\n131\t    // Each block handles one degenerate window\n132\t    DegenerateWindowMeta meta = metas[blockIdx.x];\n133\t    FpExt eq_r = meta.eq_r;\n134\t    FpExt k_rot_r = meta.k_rot_r;\n135\t    const UnstackedSlice *unstacked_cols = unstacked_cols_global + meta.col_offset;\n136\t    const FpExt *lambda_pows = lambda_pows_global + 2 * meta.col_offset;\n137\t    const FpExt *eq_ub_ptr = eq_ub_all + meta.eq_ub_offset;\n138\t    uint32_t window_len = meta.window_len;\n139\t\n140\t    FpExt local_sums[S_DEG];\n141\t#pragma unroll\n142\t    for (int i = 0; i < S_DEG; i++) {\n143\t        local_sums[i] = FpExt(0);\n144\t    }\n145\t\n146\t    for (uint32_t window_idx = threadIdx.x; window_idx < window_len; window_idx += blockDim.x) {\n147\t        UnstackedSlice s = unstacked_cols[window_idx];\n148\t        const FpExt *__restrict__ q = q_evals[s.commit_idx];\n149\t\n150\t        auto col_idx = s.stacked_col_idx;\n151\t        auto row_idx = s.stacked_row_idx;\n152\t        auto row_start = (row_idx >> shift_factor) << 1;\n153\t        auto q_offset = col_idx * q_height + row_start;\n154\t\n155\t        auto q_0 = q[q_offset];\n156\t        auto q_1 = q[q_offset + 1];\n157\t        auto q_c1 = q_1 - q_0;\n158\t\n159\t        uint32_t b_bool = (row_idx >> (shift_factor - 1)) & 1;\n160\t        Fp b = Fp(b_bool);\n161\t\n162\t        auto eq_ub = eq_ub_ptr[window_idx];\n163\t\n164\t#pragma unroll\n165\t        for (int x_int = 1; x_int <= S_DEG; ++x_int) {\n166\t            Fp x = Fp(x_int);\n167\t            auto eq_ub_x = eq_ub * eq1(x, b);\n168\t            auto eq = eq_r * eq_ub_x;\n169\t            auto k_rot = k_rot_r * eq_ub_x;\n170\t\n171\t            auto q_x = q_0 + q_c1 * x;\n172\t\n173\t            local_sums[x_int - 1] +=\n174\t                (lambda_pows[2 * window_idx] * eq + lambda_pows[2 * window_idx + 1] * k_rot) * q_x;\n175\t        }\n176\t    }\n177\t\n178\t#pragma unroll\n179\t    for (int idx = 0; idx < S_DEG; idx++) {\n180\t        FpExt reduced = sumcheck::block_reduce_sum(local_sums[idx], shared);\n181\t        if (threadIdx.x == 0) {\n182\t            sumcheck::atomic_add_fpext_to_u64(output + idx * 4, reduced);\n183\t        }\n184\t        __syncthreads();\n185\t    }\n186\t}\n187\t```\n188\t\n189\tThe inner loop body is identical to the existing degenerate kernel. The only difference is:\n190\t- `blockIdx.x` selects the window (instead of always being 0).\n191\t- Per-window parameters (`eq_r`, `k_rot_r`, pointers) are loaded from the `metas` array instead of kernel arguments.\n192\t\n193\t### Step 3: Add batched launcher\n194\t\n195\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` (after the existing degenerate launcher, around line 570)\n196\t\n197\t```c\n198\textern \"C\" int _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n199\t    const FpExt *const *q_evals,\n200\t    const FpExt *eq_ub_all,\n201\t    const UnstackedSlice *unstacked_cols,\n202\t    const FpExt *lambda_pows,\n203\t    const DegenerateWindowMeta *metas,\n204\t    uint64_t *output,\n205\t    uint32_t q_height,\n206\t    uint32_t num_windows,\n207\t    uint32_t shift_factor\n208\t) {\n209\t    if (num_windows == 0) return 0;\n210\t\n211\t    dim3 block(256);\n212\t    dim3 grid(num_windows);\n213\t    // grid.x supports up to 2^31-1 on compute capability >= 3.0\n214\t    // Atomic overflow check: num_windows * 256 * ~2^31 < 2^50 << 2^64\n215\t    size_t shmem_bytes = div_ceil(block.x, WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt);\n216\t\n217\t    stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched_kernel<<<grid, block, shmem_bytes>>>(\n218\t        q_evals, eq_ub_all, unstacked_cols, lambda_pows, metas,\n219\t        output, q_height, shift_factor\n220\t    );\n221\t\n222\t    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n223\t}\n224\t```\n225\t\n226\tBlock size is fixed at 256. Windows with `window_len < 256` have idle threads that skip the inner loop — this is a minor inefficiency but eliminates the need for per-window block size tuning. The original kernel used `min(window_len, 256)`, so the worst case is launching 256 threads for a window with 1 column. At ~3.9us average GPU time per degenerate window, this inefficiency is negligible.\n227\t\n228\t### Step 4: Add Rust FFI binding\n229\t\n230\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n231\t\n232\tAdd extern declaration (inside the existing `extern \"C\"` block):\n233\t\n234\t```rust\n235\tfn _stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n236\t    q_evals: *const *const EF,\n237\t    eq_ub_all: *const EF,\n238\t    unstacked_cols: *const UnstackedSlice,\n239\t    lambda_pows: *const EF,\n240\t    metas: *const DegenerateWindowMeta,\n241\t    output: *mut u64,\n242\t    q_height: u32,\n243\t    num_windows: u32,\n244\t    shift_factor: u32,\n245\t) -> i32;\n246\t```\n247\t\n248\tAdd safe wrapper function (after the existing `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate` wrapper):\n249\t\n250\t```rust\n251\t/// Batched degenerate case: launches one block per degenerate window, all atomically\n252\t/// accumulating into a single output buffer. The caller must zero-initialize `output`\n253\t/// before calling.\n254\t#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n255\tpub unsafe fn stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n256\t    q_evals: &DeviceBuffer<*const EF>,\n257\t    eq_ub_all: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n258\t    unstacked_cols: &DeviceBuffer<UnstackedSlice>,\n259\t    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n260\t    metas: &DeviceBuffer<DegenerateWindowMeta>,\n261\t    output: &mut DeviceBuffer<u64>,\n262\t    q_height: usize,\n263\t    num_windows: usize,\n264\t    l_skip: usize,\n265\t    round: usize,\n266\t) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n267\t    debug_assert!(output.len() >= STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG * D_EF);\n268\t\n269\t    check(_stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n270\t        q_evals.as_ptr(),\n271\t        eq_ub_all.as_ptr(),\n272\t        unstacked_cols.as_ptr(),\n273\t        lambda_pows.as_ptr(),\n274\t        metas.as_ptr(),\n275\t        output.as_mut_ptr(),\n276\t        q_height as u32,\n277\t        num_windows as u32,\n278\t        (l_skip + round) as u32,\n279\t    ))\n280\t}\n281\t```\n282\t\n283\tImport `DegenerateWindowMeta` from the parent module. Add to the existing imports at the top of the file:\n284\t\n285\t```rust\n286\tuse crate::stacked_reduction::{DegenerateWindowMeta, UnstackedSlice, STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG};\n287\t```\n288\t\n289\t(Adjust the existing `use crate::stacked_reduction::...` import to include `DegenerateWindowMeta`.)\n290\t\n291\t### Step 5: Add error variant\n292\t\n293\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/error.rs`\n294\t\n295\tAdd new variant to `StackedReductionError` enum:\n296\t\n297\t```rust\n298\t#[error(\"sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched: {0}\")]\n299\tSumcheckMleRoundDegenerateBatched(CudaError),\n300\t```\n301\t\n302\t### Step 6: Restructure `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval`\n303\t\n304\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, function `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (lines 793-912)\n305\t\n306\tReplace lines 832-911 (the per-window loop + final sum) with:\n307\t\n308\t```rust\n309\t// Phase 1: Classify windows into degenerate vs non-degenerate\n310\tlet mut degen_metas: Vec<DegenerateWindowMeta> = Vec::new();\n311\tlet mut degen_eq_ub: Vec<EF> = Vec::new();\n312\tlet mut non_degen_windows: Vec<[usize; 2]> = Vec::new();\n313\t\n314\tfor window in self.ht_diff_idxs.windows(2) {\n315\t    let window_start = window[0];\n316\t    let window_end = window[1];\n317\t    let window_len = window_end - window_start;\n318\t    let log_height = self.unstacked_cols[window_start].log_height as usize;\n319\t\n320\t    if log_height < l_skip + round {\n321\t        let eq_ub_offset = degen_eq_ub.len();\n322\t        degen_eq_ub.extend_from_slice(&self.eq_ub_per_trace[window_start..window_end]);\n323\t        degen_metas.push(DegenerateWindowMeta {\n324\t            col_offset: window_start as u32,\n325\t            eq_ub_offset: eq_ub_offset as u32,\n326\t            window_len: window_len as u32,\n327\t            _pad: 0,\n328\t            eq_r: self.eq_stable[log_height],\n329\t            k_rot_r: self.k_rot_stable[log_height],\n330\t        });\n331\t    } else {\n332\t        non_degen_windows.push([window_start, window_end]);\n333\t    }\n334\t}\n335\t\n336\t// Phase 2: Batch launch all degenerate windows\n337\tlet mut total_evals = [EF::ZERO; STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG];\n338\t\n339\tif !degen_metas.is_empty() {\n340\t    self.d_accum\n341\t        .fill_zero()\n342\t        .map_err(StackedReductionError::FillZero)?;\n343\t\n344\t    // Upload metadata\n345\t    let d_metas = degen_metas.to_device()?;\n346\t\n347\t    // Upload concatenated eq_ub values\n348\t    if degen_eq_ub.len() > self.d_eq_ub.len() {\n349\t        self.d_eq_ub = DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(degen_eq_ub.len());\n350\t    }\n351\t    degen_eq_ub.copy_to(&mut self.d_eq_ub)?;\n352\t\n353\t    let stacked_height = self.stacked_height(round);\n354\t    unsafe {\n355\t        stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched(\n356\t            &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n357\t            &self.d_eq_ub,\n358\t            &self.d_unstacked_cols,\n359\t            &self.d_lambda_pows,\n360\t            &d_metas,\n361\t            &mut self.d_accum,\n362\t            stacked_height,\n363\t            degen_metas.len(),\n364\t            l_skip,\n365\t            round,\n366\t        )\n367\t        .map_err(StackedReductionError::SumcheckMleRoundDegenerateBatched)?;\n368\t    }\n369\t\n370\t    let h_accum = self.d_accum.to_host()?;\n371\t    let degen_evals = reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(&h_accum);\n372\t    for i in 0..STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG {\n373\t        total_evals[i] += degen_evals[i];\n374\t    }\n375\t    // d_metas dropped here (stream-ordered free)\n376\t}\n377\t\n378\t// Phase 3: Per-window non-degenerate launches (keep existing logic)\n379\tfor &[window_start, window_end] in &non_degen_windows {\n380\t    let window_len = window_end - window_start;\n381\t    let unstacked_cols_ptr = unsafe { self.d_unstacked_cols.as_ptr().add(window_start) };\n382\t    let lambda_pows_ptr = unsafe { self.d_lambda_pows.as_ptr().add(2 * window_start) };\n383\t    let log_height = self.unstacked_cols[window_start].log_height as usize;\n384\t    let hypercube_dim = log_height - l_skip - round;\n385\t    let num_y = 1 << hypercube_dim;\n386\t\n387\t    self.d_accum\n388\t        .fill_zero()\n389\t        .map_err(StackedReductionError::FillZero)?;\n390\t\n391\t    let stacked_height = self.stacked_height(round);\n392\t    unsafe {\n393\t        stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round(\n394\t            &self.d_q_eval_ptrs,\n395\t            &self.eq_r_ns,\n396\t            &self.k_rot_ns,\n397\t            unstacked_cols_ptr,\n398\t            lambda_pows_ptr,\n399\t            &mut self.d_accum,\n400\t            stacked_height,\n401\t            window_len,\n402\t            num_y,\n403\t            self.sm_count,\n404\t        )\n405\t        .map_err(StackedReductionError::SumcheckMleRound)?;\n406\t    };\n407\t\n408\t    let h_accum = self.d_accum.to_host()?;\n409\t    let evals = reduce_raw_u64_to_ef(&h_accum);\n410\t    for i in 0..STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG {\n411\t        total_evals[i] += evals[i];\n412\t    }\n413\t}\n414\t\n415\tOk(total_evals)\n416\t```\n417\t\n418\tAdd to the imports at the top of `stacked_reduction.rs`:\n419\t\n420\t```rust\n421\tuse crate::cuda::stacked_reduction::stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate_batched;\n422\t```\n423\t\n424\tThe existing import of `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round_degenerate` (line 34) is no longer needed and can be removed. The existing import of `stacked_reduction_sumcheck_mle_round` (line 33) is kept for non-degenerate windows.\n425\t\n426\t### Summary of Touched Files\n427\t\n428\t| File | What changes |\n429\t|---|---|\n430\t| `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs:~150` | Add `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct |\n431\t| `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs:832-911` | Replace per-window loop with classification + batched degenerate + per-window non-degenerate |\n432\t| `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` (imports) | Add batched launcher import, remove unused degenerate import |\n433\t| `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu:~29` | Add `DegenerateWindowMeta` struct |\n434\t| `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu:~368` | Add batched degenerate kernel |\n435\t| `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu:~570` | Add batched degenerate launcher |\n436\t| `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs` | Add FFI extern declaration + safe wrapper for batched launcher |\n437\t| `crates/cuda-backend/src/error.rs` | Add `SumcheckMleRoundDegenerateBatched` variant |\n438\t\n439\tNo other files are modified. The old per-window degenerate kernel and launcher remain in the codebase (dead code) — they can be removed in a follow-up cleanup if the batched version is proven correct.\n440\t\n441\t## Invariants\n442\t\n443\t1. **Output equivalence**: The function returns `[EF; STACKED_REDUCTION_S_DEG]` computed as the sum over all windows' contributions. In the current code, each window atomically accumulates into `d_accum`, which is read back and summed on CPU. In the new code, all degenerate windows atomically accumulate into the same `d_accum` in one kernel launch, and non-degenerate windows still get their own per-window cycle. Since addition is commutative and associative over EF, the final sum is identical regardless of accumulation order.\n444\t\n445\t2. **Atomic accumulation correctness**: The batched kernel uses the same `atomic_add_fpext_to_u64` as the existing degenerate kernel. Multiple blocks writing to the same output is safe because:\n446\t   - Atomic operations are sequentially consistent on NVIDIA GPUs.\n447\t   - The u64 accumulators cannot overflow: 10,348 blocks x 256 threads x ~2^31 max per component < 2^45 << 2^64.\n448\t   - The `d_accum` buffer is zero-initialized once before the batched launch.\n449\t\n450\t3. **Memory safety**:\n451\t   - `d_metas` is a temporary `DeviceBuffer` created by `to_device()`, lives until dropped after the D2H copy. All kernel accesses complete before the drop because `to_host()` synchronizes the stream.\n452\t   - `d_eq_ub` is resized if needed to hold all degenerate eq_ub values. The resize drops the old buffer (stream-ordered free) and allocates a new one. This is safe because the old buffer is not in use.\n453\t   - `d_unstacked_cols` and `d_lambda_pows` are persistent fields, valid for the lifetime of `StackedReductionGpu`.\n454\t\n455\t4. **Kernel computation correctness**: The batched kernel's inner loop body is character-for-character identical to the existing degenerate kernel. Per-window parameters (`eq_r`, `k_rot_r`, pointers, `window_len`) are loaded from the metadata array instead of kernel arguments, but the values are the same.\n456\t\n457\t5. **Non-degenerate path unchanged**: The non-degenerate windows use the exact same code as before (same kernel, same fill_zero/to_host cycle, same auto-tuning). The only change is the loop iteration source (a pre-classified `Vec<[usize; 2]>` instead of inline classification).\n458\t\n459\t6. **Round progression correctness**: `eq_stable` and `k_rot_stable` are updated at the start of `batch_sumcheck_poly_eval` (lines 804-831, unchanged). The classification loop reads from these updated values, so each round uses the correct scalars.\n460\t\n461\t## Measurement Plan\n462\t\n463\t### Before (baseline for this task)\n464\t\n465\tRun the pairing benchmark for APC 0, 100, 300 on the current code (after the previous Round 0 optimization):\n466\t\n467\t```bash\n468\tcd /path/to/powdr\n469\topenvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh  # for each APC config\n470\t```\n471\t\n472\tCollect `metrics.json` for each config. Analyze with:\n473\t\n474\t```bash\n475\tpython spec.py results/pairing/<config>/metrics.json before_<config>\n476\t```\n477\t\n478\tRecord \"Stacked Reduction\" and \"STARK (excl. trace)\" values.\n479\t\n480\t### After\n481\t\n482\tApply the changes, then rerun the same benchmarks:\n483\t\n484\t```bash\n485\tcd /path/to/powdr\n486\topenvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh  # for each APC config\n487\t```\n488\t\n489\tCollect new `metrics.json` files. Analyze with:\n490\t\n491\t```bash\n492\tpython spec.py results/pairing/<config>/metrics.json after_<config>\n493\t```\n494\t\n495\t### What to Compare\n496\t\n497\t| Metric | APC 0 | APC 100 | APC 300 |\n498\t|---|---|---|---|\n499\t| Stacked Reduction (ms) | before vs after | before vs after | before vs after |\n500\t| STARK excl trace (ms) | before vs after | before vs after | before vs after |\n501\t| Ratio APC300/APC0 STARK excl trace | before vs after | | |\n502\t\n503\t### Correctness Verification\n504\t\n505\t```bash\n506\tcargo nextest run -p openvm-cuda-backend --test-threads=4\n507\t```\n508\t\n509\tAll existing tests must pass. The pairing benchmark itself also verifies proof correctness.\n510\t\n511\t### GPU Memory Check\n512\t\n513\tMonitor physical GPU memory during the APC 300 run using `nvidia-smi` to verify no significant peak memory increase. The per-round metadata upload is ~10K * 48 bytes = ~480KB (plus eq_ub), negligible relative to GPU memory budget.\n514\t\n515\t## Rollback Criteria\n516\t\n517\t1. **Correctness failure**: Any test failure or proof verification failure -> immediate revert.\n518\t2. **Insufficient improvement**: If Stacked Reduction APC 300 improves by less than 100ms (< 32% of ~310ms), the optimization is not delivering expected value -> revert.\n519\t3. **Regression on APC 0**: If APC 0 STARK excl trace regresses by more than 20ms -> investigate before committing.\n520\t4. **GPU memory regression**: If physical peak GPU memory (from `nvidia-smi`) increases by more than 100MB -> investigate. Per-round metadata is <1MB so this should not happen.\n521\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BREvi9ZdCNL121MQfRpHhk","session_id":"f75a9bb0-08dc-4cc2-8653-93cb45f6f821","uuid":"8cd27e7f-ad24-414a-9a86-714960f3d518","timestamp":"2026-04-10T18:20:47.480Z"}
